<p>You have probably tried AI by now. You opened a chat, typed &quot;write me an Instagram post about glute training,&quot; and got something that sounded like every other trainer online. So you closed the tab. Maybe you decided that neither you nor your clients want to hear from AI, and that it is making the world worse.</p>
<p>That result does not mean you did it wrong. It is what happens when AI knows nothing about your business. It does not know who you train, what you sell or how you talk, so it guesses. And the leads you do get still need a real person to <a href="/posts/follow-up-for-trainers/">follow up with them</a>.</p>
<p>Used well, AI can take hours of repetitive work off your plate. Used badly, it fills your feed with posts nobody believes. The difference is setup, and you do not need technical skills for it.</p>
<p>So let's get you to systemize, and to use AI as the powerful tool it is. This guide takes you from zero to one working system. You set up four things once, so AI works from and for your business. You will also see what AI cannot do for you, because that matters just as much. And for each setup, you will get a quick way to test whether it works before you rely on it.</p>
