<h2 id="what-it-means-to-use-ai-properly">What it means to use AI properly</h2>
<p>Most trainers use AI like a search box. You type a question, you get an answer, and you start from zero next time. That is fine but not very efficient or current to how businesses are using Gen AI tools now, like ChatGPT or Claude.</p>
<p>Using AI properly means giving it a standing place in your business. You teach it who you are,  what your business is about, and what you need to get done once. After that, it helps with the same jobs every business has, daily.</p>
<p>Some people promise to automate your whole business and take you from 0 to 1,000 in one webinar, for a hefty fee. This isn't that. Here, we go from 0 to 1. You keep full control of your work, and AI handles the manual tasks and helps you understand your business better. It's a smart tool, nothing more.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>01 Brand files:</strong> AI learns who you train, what you sell, and how you sound.</li>
<li><strong>02: Offer plan: </strong>AI helps you decide what you are selling right now and how to talk about it.</li>
<li><strong>03: Content repurposing:</strong> AI turns one main piece of content into posts for every social platform you use.</li>
<li><strong>04: Lead follow-up.</strong> AI helps you sort new leads and reply fast, while you stay in charge of every message.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="which-ai-setup-should-you-start-with">Which AI setup should you start with?</h2>
<p>Start with the one that fixes your biggest frustration.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="setup-choice"><colgroup><col class="situation-col" /><col class="start-col" /></colgroup><thead><tr><th scope="col">If this sounds like you</th><th scope="col">Start with</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>AI answers still do not satisfy you</td><td>Setup 1: Brand files</td></tr><tr><td>You are not sure what to create next, what to promote or how to do it</td><td>Setup 2: Offer plan</td></tr><tr><td>You rewrite the same content by hand for every platform, or you post at random</td><td>Setup 3: Content flow</td></tr><tr><td>People message you, but you reply late or inconsistently</td><td>Setup 4: Lead follow-up</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>For most trainers, Setup 1 comes first, because the other three read from it. If AI keeps sounding generic, fix that before anything else.</p>
<h2 id="what-ai-can-do-for-you-and-what-it-cannot">What AI can do for you, and what it cannot</h2>
<p>AI can get you closer to a client faster. It cannot bring you clients by itself. Here is where the line sits.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="capabilities">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> What AI can do</th><th scope="col"><span aria-hidden="true">×</span> What AI cannot do</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><ul>
        <li><span class="cell-icon yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><strong>Draft.</strong> Posts, emails, replies and scripts, in your voice once it knows your voice.</li>
